{
  "_comment": "Frozen test vectors for the login signing-input format. The Python server (and the TS client when it lands) BOTH parse this file and assert that `nonce_bytes || expires_at_iso_utf8 || device_pubkey_bytes` produces exactly the documented `signing_input_hex`. Drift in either direction — wrong concatenation order, wrong ISO format (microseconds, +00:00 vs Z, padding), wrong text encoding — fails the fixture and surfaces immediately, instead of breaking signatures silently in production.",
  "_format": {
    "nonce_hex": "lowercase hex of the 32-byte nonce",
    "expires_at_iso": "the exact ASCII string the server emits and signs over (`%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ`)",
    "device_pubkey_hex": "lowercase hex of the 32-byte Ed25519 public key",
    "signing_input_hex": "lowercase hex of `nonce_bytes || expires_at_iso_utf8 || device_pubkey_bytes`"
  },
